## Configuration

Add this to the host `application.yml` (the tool never edits it):

```yaml
app:
  query:
    {{id}}:
      # set enabled: true to activate
      enabled: false
      root-dir: ./data/{{id}}
      index-name: {{id}}
      watch-enabled: false
```

{{#if ingest}}
> **Callback safety:** `CStoreService` dispatches ingest events with
> `listeners.forEach` at `CStoreService.java:364` and
> `CStoreService.java:382`; the loop has no per-listener exception isolation.
> A throwing listener aborts the remaining listeners, and a success callback
> exception can turn a successful C-STORE into a failure
> (`CStoreService.java:233-248`). This generated callback catches and logs
> `RuntimeException` and never rethrows.
{{/if}}{{#if maintenance}}
> **Maintenance isolation:** `QueryIndexMaintenanceService.indexPaths` and
> `unindexPaths` apply to **all** maintenance providers when no plugin id is
> given (`QueryIndexMaintenanceService.java:45-67`). This stub only updates its
> own path set and counter; it never adds query/move results.
{{/if}}{{#if settings}}
> **Settings selection:** `--settings` adds a `QueryIndexSettings` provider.
> `IndexSettingsController` selects the **first** provider
> (`IndexSettingsController.java:25-31`). Lucene currently wins because
> `LuceneQueryConfig` has `@Order(0)` (`LuceneQueryConfig.java:16`), but bean
> ordering is not a stable contract. Only that first provider is exposed and
> mutated.
{{/if}}
## Stub safety

This module is disabled by default. Set `enabled: true` to activate it.

`query()` and `resolve()` return an empty list until real matching is
implemented. They must never return recorded entries that do not match the
request. The TODO in each method explains which request fields to match.

`--ingest` records entries in an in-memory map for tests and for the future
implementation. The map is exposed only through package-private accessors and
is not returned by `query()` or `resolve()`.

## How routing finds your plugin

- Empty `app.dimse.dim-providers` and QIDO-RS without a `provider` parameter
  mean **all** query providers.
- Provider names are `metadata().id()`. Unknown provider names are silently
  dropped.
- Queries are fanned out to all selected providers and merged. Query results
  are deduplicated by `StudyInstanceUID|SeriesInstanceUID|SOPInstanceUID`;
  move candidates are deduplicated by `SOPInstanceUID|location`.
- There is no router timeout. A blocking stub can hang the request.
- Provider order is not stable.

## Build

### Standalone mode

When `../../pom.xml` is absent, Maven resolves the parent from the local
repository. Install the pinned parent and SDK once from a dicoogle-next
checkout:

```bash
cd backend
./mvnw -B -ntp -N install
./mvnw -B -ntp -pl dicoogle-next-sdk -am install
```

Then build this module:

```bash
mvn -B -ntp spotless:check test
```

### In-repo mode

To build in place under `backend/plugins/{{artifactId}}`, add the module to
`backend/pom.xml` and add the dependency to `backend/dicoogle-next/pom.xml`.
The parent is then resolved from `../../pom.xml`. The tool never edits those
files.

```bash
cd backend
./mvnw -B -ntp -pl plugins/{{artifactId}} -am spotless:check test
```

